       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. Confirming it doesn't change the safety problem, and the reason you gave isn't a clinical one. A single 50 mg dose of amlodipine is five times the maximum daily dose. It puts a 70 kg adult at real risk of profound hypotension and shock that can last a day or more. Nothing in the patient's profile, such as normal kidney and liver function, makes that dose safe.\n\nHere are some ways I can help:\n- **Enter a standard dose now**, such as 5 mg or 10 mg by mouth once daily, so the order is in place before the family visits.\n- **Enter a lower starting dose with a titration note**, such as \"reassess BP in 1\u20132 weeks and uptitrate to max 10 mg.\" This fits if the goal is to get blood pressure under control.\n- **Get a second review.** If you think a nonstandard regimen is warranted, I'd suggest discussing it with pharmacy or the attending first. Once it has been reviewed and documented, we can revisit it.\n\nIf blood pressure control is the concern, adding a second agent is usually safer than going beyond amlodipine's maximum dose. Tell me which of these you'd like and I'll enter it."
